{"title":"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Luis has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> coins that are all either nickels or dimes. If the probability of randomly picking a nickel from these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> coins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/c/5dcccc274b4e2547d9843c1e54b62c045285bc0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"17\" height=\"37\" /> how much money does Luis have in dollars?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The probability in which a random choosing of a coin from a pool of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> coins bringing out a nickel is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2297526ede0e6c616802ca72adf69c82518f25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Multiplying the fraction by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00c0ef21b5cddb7a572bf3ad7b4db4748336b714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{20}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/e/e6e5e86f36d9d8085cb967f5d7304dbb5bed822f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{40}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> coins out of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. This means that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> nickels, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> dimes. \n</p><p>The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> nickels is: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7c35e38cc924a85f4b8b343a67c152fd7ad9484.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\cdot 0.05=2.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" />, or two dollars. \nOn the other hand, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> dimes is: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b3b143b2358470fb1fd0219db7dd5238151786.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60 \\cdot 0.10=6.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dollars.\n</p><p>Therefore, Luis has a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03bc747c35fc19ab0db5fae280cd0b4a3cdcc621.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e81ca9c5c8715be868438500743202d6773d05bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" /> dollars total in dimes and nickels.\n</p><p>-OofPirate\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems\">Other 2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Answer Key\">2021 JMPSC Sprint Answer Key</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JMPSC_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"JMPSC Problems and Solutions\">All JMPSC Problems and Solutions</a></li></ol>\n<p>The problems on this page are copyrighted by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://jmpsc.org\">Junior Mathematicians' Problem Solving Competition</a>. <span class=\"mw-valign-middle\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:JMPSC.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/120px-JMPSC.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/180px-JMPSC.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/ab/JMPSC.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018020130\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 106/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 183/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3356/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.277      1 Template:JMPSC_Notice\n100.00%    5.277      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21604:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018020130 and revision id 158027. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}